[32m+[m[32m## Admin payment approval UI guidance[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- The admin payment approval flow belongs in the admin orders dashboard and should follow the workflow described in ADMIN_PAYMENT_UI_GUIDE.md.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For online payment methods such as GCash or PayMaya, show the approval action only when the order is in a valid review state: payment status is PAID and order status is PENDING_PAYMENT.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Do not show payment approval buttons for cash orders; cash orders should follow the confirm/complete flow instead of a payment approval flow.[m
[32m+[m[32m- If payment is pending, failed, or cancelled, keep the payment state visible but do not allow approval.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The UI must reflect the server-backed payment and order state accurately, never assume client-side values are valid.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Do not change the meaning of payment status badges or order status labels without updating the business logic and the UI guide together.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Keep payment approval distinct from general order confirmation: approval is for online payment verification, while confirmation is for order progression or cash settlement.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Cash payment must not be treated as paid before the order reaches completion; the effective cash payment status should remain pending until the order is completed.[m
[32m+[m[32m- For future implementation work, prefer a single source of truth for order lifecycle rules instead of duplicating logic between UI, route handlers, and shared helpers.[m
